Your assertion code might be something like this:

```cs
Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX != Old_arrListLastIndexOfX, "The last position of x in old and new lists are different.");
```

The general form of Debug.Assert is Debug.Assert(cond, message), and this asserts that `cond` is true; if `cond` is false, it throws an AssertFailedException with the provided message. 

In the provided C# code, New_arrListLastIndexOfX and Old_arrListLastIndexOfX are the last index of the value to be inserted at the old and new list respectively. The Assert statement checks if they are same. If they are same, the insert operation did not change the last index of 'x' in the array list and it throws an AssertFailedException with the provided message otherwise.--------------------Here is the csharp code output based on the assert statements mentioned in the comments:

