Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount + 1 == New_arrListCount, "The count of arrList is not increased by 1 after insertion");
Debug.Assert(Old_x != New_arrList[New_arrListIndexOfX], "The values at index of x in the old and new lists do not match");
```
Note: the line with `Old_x!= New_arrList[New_arrListIndexOfX]` is not correct as it seems the operation didn't insert x but maybe was replacing some other element. So, this needs to be adapted based on your code. If you want the original value of `x` on the index after the insertion, then `Old_x` from the old state should be used instead of `New_arrList[New_arrListIndexOfX]`.--------------------